WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:08.419
Cora and Rita reached Boulder Valley.

2
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.094
"Do you see Mo?" Rita asked.

3
00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:16.131
Cora looked around. "Not yet."

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:20.785
"Maybe he's not here," Rita said.

5
00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:30.382
"The arrow is never wrong," Cora said.

6
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:34.309
Rita spotted a small fish with long spikes.

7
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:40.855
"Is that a lionfish?" she asked nervously.

8
00:00:40.856 --> 00:00:42.972
Cora nodded.

9
00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:47.599
"Will it try to eat us?" Rita asked.

10
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.017
"We're too big," Cora said.

11
00:00:51.018 --> 00:00:58.724
"But it might eat Mo."

12
00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:03.081
Cora and Rita slowly swam closer.

13
00:01:03.082 --> 00:01:07.343
"Um, hi," Cora called.

14
00:01:07.344 --> 00:01:09.986
"Have you seen our friend Mo?

15
00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:18.352
He's a porcupinefish."

16
00:01:18.353 --> 00:01:23.594
"Is he little and puffy?" the lionfish asked.

17
00:01:23.595 --> 00:01:26.428
"Yes!" Rita said.

18
00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:31.941
"I saw him." The lionfish looked around.

19
00:01:31.942 --> 00:01:37.388
"He was, uh, swimming that way."

20
00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:41.256
The lionfish pointed deeper into Boulder Valley.

21
00:01:41.257 --> 00:01:46.547
Rita frowned. "Why would Mo go there?"

22
00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:51.054
"Because . . . ," the lionfish said.

23
00:01:51.055 --> 00:01:56.797
"Some big, hungry scorpionfish were chasing him!"

24
00:01:56.798 --> 00:02:05.446
"Oh no!" Cora cried. "Let's go!"

25
00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:12.266
Cora and Rita swam off.

26
00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:17.255
Soon they spotted the big scorpionfish.

27
00:02:17.256 --> 00:02:24.602
Rita gasped. "Their spines are sharp—and scary!"

28
00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:27.900
Cora was busy looking around.

29
00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.636
Suddenly she grinned.

30
00:02:30.637 --> 00:02:38.187
'I know how to be scarier!'

